    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d287">

                <pb facs="0440" n="352" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg352"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Baron Fava to Mr. Foster.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of Italy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Lenox,
                                Mass.</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian" when="1892-08-09"
                                ><hi rendition="#italic">August 9, 1892</hi></date>. (Received
                        August 12.)</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I received just now from his excellency the
                    Italian minister of foreign affairs, the cablegram of which I have the honor to
                    forward herewith the copy.</p>
                <p>By said cablegram Mr. Brin communicates to me that, having learned the United
                    States Government’s resolution to send two men-of-war to Genoa on the occasion
                    of the royal visit to the Columbian Exhibition, His Majesty the King, my august
                    sovereign, directs me to be the interpreter of his deep gratification at this
                    renewed manifestation of the reciprocal cordiality of the friendship between the
                    two countries.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fava.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d287-a1.xml" xpointer="d287-a1"/>
